^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-20 19:00] observe — recent mounted tooling, editor plans, query machinery, and model capacity create a better moment for consolidation than for adding another metaphor-bound surface.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:01] revise — left/right becomes a renderable orientation over canonical open/close, prefix/postfix, before/after, and typed port roles; operational asymmetry requires a dialect version and tests.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:02] decide — spacing is preserved and measured as soft layout topology; explicit tokens and containers remain semantic authority.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:03] decide — claim and genomic vocabulary are optional postures or projections; Frame, Consideration, Move, Observation, Episode, and Local Universe carry the neutral contract.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:04] decide — hydration is staged as abstract plan, validated plan, capability-bound plan, preview or emitted artifact, then observed run.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:05] decide — agent contexts receive bounded evidence packets with revisions, query profile, source spans, exact and approximate tiers, contribution traces, exclusions, and cost.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:06] taste — density is nutritious when each field changes orientation, comparison, action, or falsification; repeated ambient prose is not nutrition.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:07] hygiene — current checkout is dirty main; preserve existing changes, avoid rebase and commit, and require a reviewed hygiene split before source implementation.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:08] observe — CLI canonical formatting, CLI equivalence rewrites, and LSP formatting currently follow different paths; indentation is heuristic, range context is lossy, and paired brace labels are unpopulated AST affordances.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:09] decide — layout, label, and context changes become previewable differentials with exact parser-owned targets, content-hash preconditions, source maps, vector mutation profiles, and idempotence checks.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:10] decide — indentation pulses advance one confirmed S2 batch, reparse, compare declared identities, append an observation, and stop at fixed point, failure, conflict, cancellation, or budget.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:11] research — whitespace physics will hold content and parsed structure constant, counterbalance layout profiles, and measure orientation, navigation, edit accuracy, delayed recall, and explicit familiarity separately.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:12] decide — reversible view rotations and source rewrites are distinct; review profiles disclose inverse or information loss and measure semantic signal per hunk, stable anchors, layout noise, and reviewer outcomes.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:13] probe — lattice query ?~@&*^ with braces <>{} scanned 93 .spw files and returned 20; common blocks saturated operator and brace coverage, so negative controls and exact parser-owned tiers are required before ranking claims.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:14] taste — bounded babbling is useful learner churn; candidate idioms earn promotion through exact fixtures, downstream impact packets, steward explanation, versioning, and reversible migration previews.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:15] decide — (), [], {}, <...>, specialized pairs, and the explicit <> operator belong to one proposed semantic coupling family while retaining distinct lexer and AST forms.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:16] math — implement a tagged recursive boundary view first; test colored-operad composition and common <> lowering only after pair identity, source maps, and parser-to-ONF goldens exist.
 >>[2026-07-20 21:42] implement — added a read-only Seed-backed topography scanner with revision-portable evidence, recovered-Prose disclosure, paired-container depth, separate explicit-couple counts, lexical-closure guards, deterministic corpus order, and focused probes
 >>[2026-07-20 22:17] decide — implemented one tagged coupling algebra with operator and paired-boundary forms; shared open-boundary kinematics preserve capsule, scope, frame, body, stream, and range kinds while physical dynamics remain named profiles
 >>[2026-07-20 22:17] implement — made flow observations profile-explicit and parse-health-aware, replaced self-equivalence with a two-source structural projection verifier, and added ambiguity, nesting, and recovery controls
 >>[2026-07-20 22:23] implement — added revisioned coupling semantic profiles with disclosed kind sets, valid port roles, measurable dimensions, falsifiers, dynamics, effect grades, and non-destructive structural projection
 >>[2026-07-21] observe — coupling occupancy/payload, form-ladders, form-geometry mobility/HOF, mutation automata, pulse CLI, topography probes, and liminality bridge landed in seed/runtime/cli.
 >>[2026-07-21] decide — editor projection of topography/geometry is owned by form-geometry-editor (roadmap 0c), not a parallel topography server model.
 >>[2026-07-21] revise — remaining topography hard gaps: parser pair_id/open_close labels; Stream without ? borrow; LSP TextEdit parity with pulse.
 >>[2026-07-20 22:48] implement — added revisioned paired-boundary form catalogs, pure mobility geometry, and evidence-bearing contour expansion/reduction with explicit loss and restoration receipts
 >>[2026-07-21 06:29] revise — mobility applications now expose parse/topography/inverse receipts; header-to-register projection refuses payload loss; register promotion remains an explicit effect.l1.memory profile (not syntax-driven)
 >>[2026-08-24 11:11] revise — the earlier spacing-soft decision governs raw width and layout evidence. Under a declared syntax.gap-affinity/1 capability, presence and newline gap classes may be semantic; crossing classes is a migration, not formatting.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:12] decide — semantic and plan identity use the declared association/gap projection, while surface and layout identity retain raw trivia. Both identities are required and neither substitutes for the other.
 >>[2026-09-05] observe — proposed focus_record facet: revision-addressed selection for inspect/cite/follow. Details in docs/research/spw/navigable-focus.spw; not an implementation commit.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:32] revise — commits reconciled: engine, scanner, contours and theory landed (hashes in done); ~[7] editor projection moved to form-geometry-editor per 07-21 decision; added ~[9] pair-label population (the card next); rotation_algebra sharpened with the measured 10-of-23 inverse count; pair_labels_ast sharpened (fields exist in nodes.ts, nothing sets them); generic wonder replaced
 >>[2026-10-12 14:32] observe — MOBILITY_RULES: 23 rules, 10 with an inverse, no dangling or asymmetric pairs, all 23 have apply
 >>[2026-10-12 15:24] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 10 landed, 4 planned, 1 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:24] observe — Two files this plan created are gone: packages/spw-seed/src/canonical/operator-ladders.ts was deleted in ca9ae1bd as a re-export no file imported, and scripts/spw-pulse.ts went in b7c5c7df when spw:pulse moved to packages/spw-cli/src/pulse.ts. The VS Code custom requests live at extensions/vscode-spw/src/lsp/custom-requests.ts (since 221128f5), not src/custom-requests.ts. PLAN.md Files and the shared hot files now say so.
 >>[2026-11-12 15:01] observe — For ?[pair_labels_ast], measured 2026-11-12 by an opt-in pass beside the parser (pair-label-reading, scanPairLabels): this repo's .spw surfaces hold 12 pairs labeled at both ends, every close repeated and none crossing, and 10 labels on an open that closes on a bare brace; populating openLabel and closeLabel would change how those 22 places and five lines in a story consumer read, and no other line. A mounted consumer's plans read labeled braces as overlapping scopes, which fields on tree nodes cannot hold: the pass reports each crossing, so a grammar rule could set the fields where a pair nests and leave an overlap to a list beside the tree. wonder_trial_pair_label holds the readings.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] note — Owner direction 2026-11-13 asks for physical agility in small steps: one physical quantity made countable from data that exists, before any is tied to a host. This plan takes the count, since coupling.ts already holds CouplingProfileStatus (interpretive, measured, operational) and a dimension with a method and a falsifier; precipitate-model-alignment takes the ledger of physical words.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — Nothing ties a parsed container to a field site today. packages/spw-seed/src/math/field.ts is imported only by math/index.ts; idioms.ts names it in strings and formula-scan.ts matches its words by regex. docs/theory/spw/field-dynamics.spw lists path-ref to field sites under proposed. The coupling.ts header keeps charge, capacitance and permeability out of Seed facts.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] decide — The first quantity is a count named body outbound: the references written inside a brace body that point outside it. The word reuses outbound in packages/spw-lsp/src/handlers/reference-graph.ts and outDegree in math/corpus.ts, which count the same thing per file. Not crossing (pair-labels.ts uses it for two pairs that overlap), not leak (spw authority uses it for a subject that does what its surface never said), not egress (brace-physics gives it to the close of a stream).
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — Definition as probed. A body is a curly pair from scanPairLabels, whole or loose. A path ref is a tilde touching a string or an angle open, and is out by definition since its target is another address. A name reference is an at-sign touching an identifier with no colon after it; its binding is the same at-name followed by a colon outside square brackets, anywhere in the same file. A name stays when a binding lies in the same body, is out when a binding lies only elsewhere in the file, and is unbound when the file binds it nowhere. Each reference is counted once, on the innermost body that holds it.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] verify — Fixture of three bodies (bound and used in one body, bound in a sibling, bound nowhere) read stay 1, out 1, unbound 1, and a nested use read out on the inner body only.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — Measured over 1,312 tracked .spw files (git ls-files, without _archive, node_modules and .claude): 32,155 bodies, 10 of them loose. Path refs out per body: 75.3% of bodies have none, median 0, ninetieth percentile 1, ninety-ninth 6, maximum 50; sum 15,924, and with the 186 written outside any body that is the 16,110 the files hold. Name references: 3,183 written, 2,498 out, 1 stays, 655 unbound, 29 outside any body; 98.2% of bodies have none out, median 0, maximum 243.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — The same count without .spw/caches, which is generated: 643 files, 10,692 bodies, 85.7% with no path ref out, median 0, ninety-ninth percentile 9, maximum 50, sum 5,258; names 2,261 out and 1 stays; 81.4% of bodies have neither kind out. The two largest bodies by names out are in .agents/plans/index.spw (243 and 242), a generated table.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] surprise — Of 2,499 name references whose binding the file holds, one is used in the body that binds it. A body in these surfaces does not bind the names it uses: handles are bound in one frame and used in the others. So a share let through is near 1 for every body that has names at all, and the quantity that varies is the count out, not a ratio.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] note — Breaks, where body outbound stops being like flux. No gradient: no body carries an amplitude, so permeability times gradient has nothing to multiply. No sign: only out is counted, and in needs a target resolved to a body. Not conserved: writing a reference adds one out and takes nothing from anywhere. Does not add under nesting: counted on every enclosing body the path refs sum to 25,907 against 15,924 written, and only the innermost count sums to the file. Path refs are out by definition and names are out by test, so the two columns are kept apart and never summed into one number.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] revise — Six planned commits added ahead of evidence_packets, one change each with its proof: count_body_outbound, outbound_sums_to_file, outbound_in_measure, outbound_dimension, inbound_by_anchor, outbound_host_packet. Card next and next_commit now name count_body_outbound; populate_pair_labels keeps its place and its question. Opened outbound_columns and outbound_host.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[rotation_algebra]: "MOBILITY_RULES holds 23 rules and only 10 declare an inverse; which of the other 13 are lossy projections that must say so in their receipt, and which are merely unpaired?"
 ?[pair_labels_ast]: "Should the container grammar populate openLabel/closeLabel on Frame, Body and Scope now (the fields exist in types/ast/nodes.ts, nothing sets them), or wait for parser-to-ONF goldens of pair identity?"
 ?[outbound_columns]: "Does body outbound keep path refs and name references as two columns (path refs are out by definition, names by test), or does the owner want one number; and do generated surfaces (.spw/caches, the plan index) count in the figure a host is shown?"
 ?[outbound_host]: "Which host reads the count first: a canvas host that already keeps position, velocity, heat and a sentence per tie, or the spoken form; and on the canvas, is a region the same thing as a brace body, so that a tie with its ends in two regions is one outbound reference?"
}

